AB  - A new distribution map is provided for Moniliophthora roreri (Cif.) H. C. Evans, Stalpers, Samson & Benny (Basidiomycota: Agaricales). The main host is cocoa ( Theobroma cacao ). Information is given on the geographical distribution in North America (Mexico), Central America and Caribbean (Belize, Costa Rica, Cuba, Guatemala, Honduras, Nicaragua and Panama) and South America (Colombia, Ecuador, Peru and Venezuela). There are no official records of the presence of M. roreri in neighbouring countries (Brazil and Bolivia), but it may have already invaded wild Theobroma and Herrania spp. populations or isolated cocoa plantings in these countries. M. roreri has been detected less than 50 km from the cocoa growing region in Para, Brazil.
